Desilium for Debian-style systems
=================================

The packaging here is distribution-neutral: packaging/install.sh copies the release binaries,
the session file, the portal preferences, the desktop entries and the wallpapers into a prefix.
A Debian source package should use the same script instead of hand-written install rules:

  - Build-Depends: cargo, rustc (or rustup), pkgconf, libwayland-dev, libxkbcommon-dev,
    libglib2.0-dev, libfontconfig-dev
  - Depends: libwayland-client0, libxkbcommon0, libfontconfig1, fonts-inter, kitty, libglib2.0-0t64,
    dbus-user-session | dbus-x11
  - Depends (the compositor): kwin-wayland, kglobalacceld, kf6-kconfig-bin (kwriteconfig6),
    xwayland, breeze-icon-theme (KDE's default icon theme)
  - Recommends: xdg-desktop-portal-kde, xdg-desktop-portal-gtk, breeze
  - Recommends: gvfs-backends, udisks2, network-manager, wireplumber, bluez, brightnessctl, power-profiles-daemon
  - In debian/rules, run: cargo build --release --locked -p desilium-session -p desilium-kwin
    -p desilium-shell -p desilium-settings -p desilium-notifications -p desilium-files, then
    DESTDIR=debian/tmp packaging/install.sh --prefix /usr

Use the package names of the release you target. The KDE package names above are from memory and
have not been checked against a Debian archive; KWin must be a Plasma 6 build (kwin-wayland 6.x).
The session file belongs to the desilium package, so display managers pick it up from
/usr/share/wayland-sessions/desilium.desktop without further configuration.
